concepts.content:
The **cross-attention** layer (`cross-attn`) addresses the question of how to insert image tokens into a text model. The answer is to let the text tokens attend to the image tokens. The image tokens emit their value vectors, which are mixed with the text token value vectors according to the attention weights. The equations for a cross-attention layer are:
$$\begin{aligned}
    \mathbf{Q}_{t} = \mathbf{T}_{t}\mathbf{W}_{t,q}^\mathsf{T}\\
    \mathbf{K}_{\ell} = \mathbf{T}_{\ell}\mathbf{W}_{\ell,k}^\mathsf{T}\\
    \mathbf{V}_{\ell} = \mathbf{T}_{\ell}\mathbf{W}_{\ell,v}^\mathsf{T}\\
    \mathbf{A}_{\texttt{cross}} = \texttt{softmax}(\frac{\mathbf{Q}_{t}\mathbf{K}_{\ell}^\mathsf{T}}{\sqrt{m}})\\
    \mathbf{T}_{\texttt{out}, \texttt{cross}} = \mathbf{A}_{\texttt{cross}}\mathbf{V}_{\ell}
\end{aligned}$$
where variables subscripted with $t$ are associated with text tokens and variables subscripted with $\ell$ are associated with image tokens. The output can be combined with self-attention via weighted summation:
$$\begin{aligned}
    \mathbf{T} = w_{\texttt{cross}}\mathbf{T}_{\texttt{out}, \texttt{cross}}  + w_{\texttt{self}}\mathbf{T}_{\texttt{out}, \texttt{self}}
\end{aligned}$$
where $\mathbf{T}_{\texttt{out}, \texttt{self}}$ is regular self-attention on the input text token $\mathbf{T}_t$.

